    {"id": "p0-spine-2", "milestone": "M0", "rows": ["m0-spine-selftest"], "globs": ["primitives/*", "rust/justfile", ".gitlab-ci.yml"], "deps": ["p0-dispatch", "p0-spine"], "state": "parked", "model": "opus", "title": "Spine follow-ups, each a claim proved in m0-spine-selftest (`just gate-selftest` plants each bad input and asserts the specific refusal): (S1) score.sh applies green() whenever the log has a `test result:` line, so a row whose cmd is not cargo test and prints one with 0 passed scores FAIL; (S2) own.sh has no fallback to the branch's own queue and reads own.sh and queue.json from origin/main's tip, and CI writes own.sh to a file and fails if git show fails; (S3) own.sh reads states from main's tip. A standing item (privileged=(p0-spine p0-queue) in own.sh on main) is admitted when running, review or landed, and refused when parked. Every other item is admitted only when running or review, and refused when ready, landed, parked or needs_decision. The dispatcher lands an item's flip to running on main before that item's first MR. (S3b) Privilege comes only from that list, never from an id prefix or a branch name. A standing id is refused on every item/ branch, and item/<id> is judged as <id> only when <id> is not standing. (S4) check-ownership runs on every MR whose target is main, from any source. A non-item branch is judged only through the exact map in own.sh on main: primitives/spine -> p0-spine; primitives/queue -> p0-queue; primitives/oracle-jose -> p0-oracle-jose; primitives/oracle-webauthn-ext -> p0-oracle-webauthn-ext. Any other branch is refused, prefix lookalikes included (primitives/spine-x, primitives/queue2). (S4q) p0-queue is a standing item with globs primitives/queue.json and primitives/rows.json, and for it neither file is oracle. The map, the lists and own.sh change only under p0-spine. (S4a) An MR from primitives/spine or primitives/queue merges only with a recorded pass from a verify agent that did not write it. The MR that first lands S2 to S4 is judged by main's older gate, so its verify pass runs `just gate-selftest` against the branch's own.sh. (S4b) An oracle item (oracle=(p0-oracle-jose p0-oracle-webauthn-ext) in own.sh on main) follows S3's ordinary states. It may change only rust/vectors/*, never a path matching *expected-fail* or */exam/*, and only from its mapped branch. For it, this rule replaces both the oracle-path check and its globs. (S4c) This item is never dispatched to an item/ branch; it lands on primitives/spine as p0-spine. Selftest plants: a standing id admitted while landed and refused while parked; item/p0-spine; primitives/spine-x; a non-standing item while ready; an oracle item touching rust/vectors/x/expected-fail.txt. (S5) twins fails when it checked no pair, as with a crate set with no ui crate; (S6) just deps runs cargo tree with --target all, so a target-gated dependency is listed in deps.txt; (S8) the ARCHITECTURE.md Tracked line also names the clippy.toml expose removal and the base expose feature; just api passes on its first run once the regenerated public-api.txt is staged, or says so before failing"},
